                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "102d53fd-7a2f-35c6-8cb9-58cef8f97b3e",
                        "entry_id": "94086616-f839-3168-869e-dde43f332e49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various specific theophanies.",
                            "One of the Great Feasts of the Eastern Orthodox Church, commemorating the revelation of Jesus' divinity, especially in his baptism by John the Baptist."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "64a42b44-313f-44c2-a52f-adefc4d0b1d4",
                                "sense_id": "102d53fd-7a2f-35c6-8cb9-58cef8f97b3e",
                                "text": "The Byzantine tradition concentrates all the birth narratives, including the Magi, at Christmas. Theophany is very much the feast of the Baptism of Christ, being marked by the very important ceremony of the great Blessing of Water[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1b6585d-23f8-449a-99aa-2698f3bfb557",
                                "sense_id": "102d53fd-7a2f-35c6-8cb9-58cef8f97b3e",
                                "text": "Originally, the feast of Theophany included Christ's birth, the adoration of the Magi, and Christ's childhood narratives, such as his circumcision and his presentation in the temple. It also included his baptism and the wedding at Cana[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
